@* Light / dark / auto theme menu (P14) for the public navbar and AdminLayout. Plain static markup: js/theme.js applies
   the theme before the page paints, and js/public.js handles the menu with delegated clicks, so it also works in the
   static admin layout and after enhanced navigation. site.scss hides it until theme.js has run (html[data-bs-theme]),
   so readers without JavaScript never see a menu that can't work. *@
<li class="nav-item dropdown theme-toggle">
    <button class="btn btn-link nav-link dropdown-toggle d-flex align-items-center gap-2" type="button" id="theme-toggle"
            data-bs-toggle="dropdown" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Color theme">
        <span class="bi bi-circle-half" data-theme-icon aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="d-lg-none">Theme</span>
    </button>
    <ul class="dropdown-menu dropdown-menu-end" aria-labelledby="theme-toggle">
        <li>
            <button type="button" class="dropdown-item d-flex align-items-center gap-2" data-theme-value="light" aria-pressed="false">
                <span class="bi bi-sun-fill" aria-hidden="true"></span> Light
            </button>
        </li>
        <li>
            <button type="button" class="dropdown-item d-flex align-items-center gap-2" data-theme-value="dark" aria-pressed="false">
                <span class="bi bi-moon-stars-fill" aria-hidden="true"></span> Dark
            </button>
        </li>
        <li>
            <button type="button" class="dropdown-item d-flex align-items-center gap-2" data-theme-value="auto" aria-pressed="true">
                <span class="bi bi-circle-half" aria-hidden="true"></span> Auto
            </button>
        </li>
    </ul>
</li>
